JOB-1767857046339-ng1vmpu7r	743ef9d1-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1767857032741-fivhbewkb	278.010.01	Impressed current systems No.01	MKR-IN-00071	Impressed Current Cathodic Protection (ICCP), Inspection - 1M	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Calendar	\N	1	Months	\N	\N	\N	\N	05-Jul-2025	05-Aug-2025	\N	\N	Low	No	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\nCarry out a routine monthly inspection of the Impressed Current Cathodic Protection (ICCP) system to ensure effective corrosion protection of the vessel’s hull and appendages, proper system operation, and early detection of faults or abnormal conditions.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\nCarry out a routine monthly inspection of the Impressed Current Cathodic Protection (ICCP) system to ensure effective corrosion protection of the vessel’s hull and appendages, proper system operation, and early detection of faults or abnormal conditions.	Chief Engineer	Engine	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	vessel	278.010.YY	\N	\N	No	t	\N	\N	2026-01-08 07:24:06.340507	\N	2026-01-08 07:24:06.358
JOB-1767857046362-0h65rzo34	743ef9d1-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1767857032748-kjsh4kyi0	285.001.01	Ballast tanks/SW tanks No.01	MKR-IN-00072	Ballast Tanks Inspection - 1M	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Calendar	\N	1	Months	\N	\N	\N	\N	05-Jul-2025	05-Aug-2025	\N	\N	Low	No	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\nCarry out a routine monthly inspection of ballast tanks to ensure structural integrity, coating condition, corrosion protection, and operational readiness, and to identify any signs of leakage, corrosion, or contamination at an early stage.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\nCarry out a routine monthly inspection of ballast tanks to ensure structural integrity, coating condition, corrosion protection, and operational readiness, and to identify any signs of leakage, corrosion, or contamination at an early stage.	Chief Engineer	Engine	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	vessel	285.001.YY	\N	\N	No	t	\N	\N	2026-01-08 07:24:06.363686	\N	2026-01-08 07:24:06.439
JOB-1767857046443-mll4g3fyb	743ef9d1-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1767857032353-yopu9l33d	401.005	Rudders w/nozzle	MKR-IN-00041	Rudder, Visual Check - 1M	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Calendar	\N	1	Months	\N	\N	\N	\N	05-Dec-2025	05-Jan-2026	\N	\N	Medium	Yes	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nJOB REFERENCE DETAILS\r\n===================\r\nManual Name: H-6 SHILLING RUDDER (MAKER PLAN);5303.pdf\r\nPdf Page No: 27\r\nChapter: 3. Check And Repair\r\n\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Disassemble the casing and seal ring carefully, following safety protocols.\r\n2. Inspect the condition of the mating faces for any signs of wear or damage, ensuring they are clean and properly aligned.\r\n3. Measure the leakage volume and, if applicable, check the water -injection volume to confirm it is within operational parameters.\r\nNote:\r\nCarry out this job when any leakage is found.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nJOB REFERENCE DETAILS\r\n===================\r\nManual Name: H-6 SHILLING RUDDER (MAKER PLAN);5303.pdf\r\nPdf Page No: 27\r\nChapter: 3. Check And Repair\r\n\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Disassemble the casing and seal ring carefully, following safety protocols.\r\n2. Inspect the condition of the mating faces for any signs of wear or damage, ensuring they are clean and properly aligned.\r\n3. Measure the leakage volume and, if applicable, check the water -injection volume to confirm it is within operational parameters.\r\nNote:\r\nCarry out this job when any leakage is found.	Chief Engineer	Engine	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	vessel	401.005.YY	\N	\N	Yes	t	\N	\N	2026-01-08 07:24:06.444744	\N	2026-01-08 07:24:06.444744
JOB-1767857046654-8wo8acurl	743ef9d1-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1767857032825-cnxmyk6d1	601.002.01	ME cylinder covers w/valves No.01	MKR-IN-00075	Main Engine – Cylinder Covers with Valves Inspection - 4000H	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Running Hours	\N	4000	Hours	4000	\N	\N	\N	05-Jul-2025	\N	0	4000	Low	No	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Cylinder Cover Condition\r\n\r\nInspect cylinder cover externally for cracks, corrosion, or hot spots.\r\n\r\nCheck for leakage of combustion gas, cooling water, or lube oil.\r\n\r\nVerify tightening condition of cover studs and nuts (visual/record check).\r\n\r\n2. Cooling Water Passages\r\n\r\nCheck cooling water inlet and outlet connections for leakage.\r\n\r\nMonitor jacket water temperature differences across cylinders.\r\n\r\nInspect for signs of scaling or blockage (based on temperature trend).\r\n\r\n3. Valves (Exhaust / Inlet / Starting / Indicator)\r\n\r\nInspect exhaust valve housing area for gas leakage or abnormal heating.\r\n\r\nCheck operation of:\r\n\r\nExhaust valve (opening/closing behavior via parameters)\r\n\r\nStarting air valve (no leakage during normal running)\r\n\r\nIndicator valve (tightness and free operation)\r\n\r\nEnsure valve caps and securing devices are properly fitted.\r\n\r\n4. Valve Actuation System\r\n\r\nInspect hydraulic or mechanical valve actuation components.\r\n\r\nCheck for oil leakage at pipes, flanges, and fittings.\r\n\r\nMonitor hydraulic oil pressure and temperature (if applicable).\r\n\r\n1. General Condition\r\n\r\nInspect engine exterior for oil, fuel, water, or exhaust gas leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck for abnormal vibration, noise, or overheating.\r\n\r\nEnsure foundation bolts, holding-down bolts, and chocks show no abnormal condition.\r\n\r\n2. Lubrication System\r\n\r\nCheck sump oil level and condition.\r\n\r\nReview lube oil pressure, temperature, and differential pressure across filters.\r\n\r\nInspect lube oil filters and coolers for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify oil mist detector operation and alarm status.\r\n\r\n3. Fuel System\r\n\r\nInspect fuel pumps, injectors, and fuel lines for leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck fuel oil pressure, temperature, and viscosity (as applicable).\r\n\r\nDrain and check fuel filters and settling system as required.\r\n\r\n4. Cooling Water System\r\n\r\nCheck jacket water pressure, temperature, and expansion tank level.\r\n\r\nInspect freshwater and seawater pumps for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify cooler condition and seawater inlet/outlet temperatures.\r\n\r\n5. Air & Exhaust System\r\n\r\nInspect turbocharger casing, air inlet filters, and ducting.\r\n\r\nCheck exhaust manifold for leakage, cracks, or insulation damage.\r\n\r\nMonitor exhaust gas temperatures for cylinder deviation.\r\n\r\n6. Starting & Control System\r\n\r\nCheck starting air pressure and drain receivers.\r\n\r\nInspect starting valves and control air system.\r\n\r\nVerify correct operation of engine control system, telegraph, and safety interlocks.\r\n\r\n7. Safety & Protection Devices\r\n\r\nTest safety devices as per PMS schedule:\r\n\r\nOverspeed trip\r\n\r\nLow lube oil pressure alarm\r\n\r\nHigh jacket water temperature alarm\r\n\r\nVerify crankcase relief valves condition.\r\n\r\n8. Performance Monitoring\r\n\r\nRecord engine RPM, load, and fuel consumption.\r\n\r\nReview trends for lube oil consumption and exhaust temperatures.\r\n\r\nCompare readings with previous records.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Cylinder Cover Condition\r\n\r\nInspect cylinder cover externally for cracks, corrosion, or hot spots.\r\n\r\nCheck for leakage of combustion gas, cooling water, or lube oil.\r\n\r\nVerify tightening condition of cover studs and nuts (visual/